{
  "email": "james.oconnor@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Identify sender, devices, and account status for slow file share ticket"
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-DT-0108",
  "reason": "KB-015/KB-017 quick check: disk space, uptime, warnings"
}

{
  "user_id": 8,
  "reason": "Determine whether user is on VPN/remote or office network"
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, sorry things are slow today. I checked your computer and it has plenty of free disk space, so that isn't the cause. To find out what is, could you tell me: 1) Are you in the office today or working from home on VPN? 2) Is it only the shared drives that are slow, or are websites, email and Teams slow too? 3) Is it one shared drive or folder in particular? If so, which one? 4) Are coworkers near you having the same problem? 5) Which computer are you using? Our records show your desktop (BL-DT-0108) hasn't connected to our network since early on the 11th. While you check, here are some things to try: if you're on VPN, disconnect and reconnect it. Shared drives are always a bit slower over VPN, so large files open faster from OneDrive or SharePoint. Pause any big uploads or downloads, like OneDrive sync or backups. If you're on Wi-Fi, use a cable or move closer to the access point if you can. If the computer hasn't been restarted in a few days, restart it. Reply with your answers and we'll take it from there.",
  "internal_note": "P3 slow file shares, vague report (\"everything is slow\"). User: James O'Connor (id 8), Ops Warehouse Supervisor, Chicago, hours 06:00-14:00. Device BL-DT-0108 (desktop, Win11): disk 78.1% free, no warnings, so KB-017 doesn't apply. Device shows OFFLINE, last check-in 2026-10-11T01:03Z. The user may be on a different machine, or the agent may have stopped checking in, so I asked which computer he's using. Sign-in logs show a normal pattern: he alternates between corporate network (m365) and residential VPN on different days, all Chicago, MFA OK, no failures, nothing suspicious. I couldn't tell from the logs whether he's on VPN or in the office today. Following KB-015 quick checks, I asked: office or VPN, file shares only or everything, which share, whether coworkers are affected. I gave the KB-015 fix steps. Escalate per KB-015 if the whole office is slow or one share is slow for everyone.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-015",
    "KB-017"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
